{
 "fps": 30,
 "lead": 0.8,
 "tail": 2.0,
 "footer": "Sources: canada.ca \u00b7 CRA T4002 and form T2125; self-employed filing and payment dates; instalment due dates; GST/HST small supplier and registration \u00b7 Examples, general info, not advice",
 "vo": [
  {
   "id": "L1",
   "file": "vo/L1.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Maya made fourteen thousand dollars from photography, on weekends, on top of her full-time job."
  },
  {
   "id": "L2",
   "file": "vo/L2.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Clients paid her by e-transfer. Nobody took a single dollar of tax off."
  },
  {
   "id": "L3",
   "file": "vo/L3.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "So next spring, the C R A will want about three thousand, one hundred and fifteen dollars of income tax on it. Possibly plus C P P."
  },
  {
   "id": "L4",
   "file": "vo/L4.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "And one simple habit cut that bill by one thousand, one hundred and eighty-six dollars."
  },
  {
   "id": "L5",
   "file": "vo/L5.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "By the end of this video, you'll know exactly what gets taxed on a side hustle in Canada, how much, when you pay, and the one number that changes the rules: thirty thousand dollars."
  },
  {
   "id": "L6",
   "file": "vo/L6.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "All numbers: twenty twenty-six, Ontario, a seventy thousand dollar salary. Examples, not real people. General information, not advice."
  },
  {
   "id": "L7",
   "file": "vo/L7.mp3",
   "gap": 1.0,
   "text": "First: what counts."
  },
  {
   "id": "L8",
   "file": "vo/L8.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "If you sell a service or a product to make money, regularly, that's business income. Photography, tutoring, deliveries, crafts, freelancing."
  },
  {
   "id": "L9",
   "file": "vo/L9.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "It doesn't matter how you're paid. Cash, e-transfer, an app, a platform. It's all income."
  },
  {
   "id": "L10",
   "file": "vo/L10.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "And it doesn't matter if you get a slip. Your employer sends you a T four. Your clients usually send you nothing."
  },
  {
   "id": "L11",
   "file": "vo/L11.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Business income is reported on your own return, on a form called the T twenty-one twenty-five, the Statement of Business or Professional Activities."
  },
  {
   "id": "L12",
   "file": "vo/L12.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "That's where you show what you earned, and what it cost you to earn it."
  },
  {
   "id": "L13",
   "file": "vo/L13.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "If you skip it, the income doesn't disappear. It's just missing from your return."
  },
  {
   "id": "L14",
   "file": "vo/L14.mp3",
   "gap": 1.0,
   "text": "Now, the number that's actually taxed."
  },
  {
   "id": "L15",
   "file": "vo/L15.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "You're not taxed on what you sold. You're taxed on your profit."
  },
  {
   "id": "L16",
   "file": "vo/L16.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Maya's clients paid her fourteen thousand dollars."
  },
  {
   "id": "L17",
   "file": "vo/L17.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "To earn it, she spent four thousand: editing software, website hosting, printing, and driving to shoots."
  },
  {
   "id": "L18",
   "file": "vo/L18.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Fourteen thousand, minus four thousand. Her profit is ten thousand dollars."
  },
  {
   "id": "L19",
   "file": "vo/L19.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "That ten thousand is added to her income, on top of her seventy thousand dollar salary."
  },
  {
   "id": "L20",
   "file": "vo/L20.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "The expenses have to be real, and they have to be for earning the business income. Keep every receipt. The C R A can ask to see them."
  },
  {
   "id": "L21",
   "file": "vo/L21.mp3",
   "gap": 1.0,
   "text": "Now, the bill. Here's what the profit really costs."
  },
  {
   "id": "L22",
   "file": "vo/L22.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Ten thousand dollars of profit, on top of a seventy thousand dollar salary in Ontario."
  },
  {
   "id": "L23",
   "file": "vo/L23.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Her income tax goes up by about three thousand, one hundred and fifteen dollars. About thirty-one percent of her profit."
  },
  {
   "id": "L24",
   "file": "vo/L24.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Because a side hustle sits on top of your job, it's taxed at your highest rate. Every dollar of it."
  },
  {
   "id": "L25",
   "file": "vo/L25.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "So the same side hustle costs different people different amounts."
  },
  {
   "id": "L26",
   "file": "vo/L26.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "If Maya's job paid forty-five thousand, the tax on the same ten thousand dollars of profit would be about two thousand and eighty-three dollars."
  },
  {
   "id": "L27",
   "file": "vo/L27.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "If her job paid one hundred and ten thousand, about three thousand, six hundred and eighty-nine."
  },
  {
   "id": "L28",
   "file": "vo/L28.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Same photos. Same clients. Your salary decides the rate on your side hustle."
  },
  {
   "id": "L29",
   "file": "vo/L29.mp3",
   "gap": 1.0,
   "text": "Now, the receipts."
  },
  {
   "id": "L30",
   "file": "vo/L30.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "If Maya had forgotten her expenses and reported the full fourteen thousand, the tax would be about four thousand, three hundred and one."
  },
  {
   "id": "L31",
   "file": "vo/L31.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Tracking four thousand dollars of expenses saved her one thousand, one hundred and eighty-six dollars."
  },
  {
   "id": "L32",
   "file": "vo/L32.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "That's the habit. Not a trick. Just records."
  },
  {
   "id": "L33",
   "file": "vo/L33.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "A shoebox works. A spreadsheet works. What matters is that every expense has a receipt, and a business reason."
  },
  {
   "id": "L34",
   "file": "vo/L34.mp3",
   "gap": 1.0,
   "text": "Now, the surprise most people get."
  },
  {
   "id": "L35",
   "file": "vo/L35.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "On a paycheque, tax comes off every two weeks. On a side hustle, nothing comes off."
  },
  {
   "id": "L36",
   "file": "vo/L36.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "So the whole bill shows up at once, when you file. For Maya, about three thousand, one hundred and fifteen dollars."
  },
  {
   "id": "L37",
   "file": "vo/L37.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "If she's already spent the money by April, that's a balance owing she can't pay. That's how a good year turns into a stressful one."
  },
  {
   "id": "L38",
   "file": "vo/L38.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "The simple fix: set money aside as you earn it. For Maya, that's about two hundred and sixty dollars a month."
  },
  {
   "id": "L39",
   "file": "vo/L39.mp3",
   "gap": 1.0,
   "text": "Then there's C P P. This one catches a lot of people off guard."
  },
  {
   "id": "L40",
   "file": "vo/L40.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "When you work for someone, your employer pays half of your C P P, and you pay the other half."
  },
  {
   "id": "L41",
   "file": "vo/L41.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "When you work for yourself, there's no employer. So on self-employment income, you pay both halves yourself."
  },
  {
   "id": "L42",
   "file": "vo/L42.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "How much depends on how much C P P you already paid through your job. If your job already got you to the yearly maximum, there may be little or nothing left to pay."
  },
  {
   "id": "L43",
   "file": "vo/L43.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "But don't assume. Check it on your return before you spend the money."
  },
  {
   "id": "L44",
   "file": "vo/L44.mp3",
   "gap": 1.0,
   "text": "Now, the dates."
  },
  {
   "id": "L45",
   "file": "vo/L45.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "If you or your spouse had self-employment income, you have until June fifteenth to file your return."
  },
  {
   "id": "L46",
   "file": "vo/L46.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "But here's the catch. Any balance you owe is still due on April thirtieth. Interest starts after that, even though the return isn't late."
  },
  {
   "id": "L47",
   "file": "vo/L47.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "And if you owe tax year after year, the C R A may ask you to pay in instalments. The due dates are March fifteenth, June fifteenth, September fifteenth and December fifteenth."
  },
  {
   "id": "L48",
   "file": "vo/L48.mp3",
   "gap": 1.0,
   "text": "And now, the thirty thousand dollar line."
  },
  {
   "id": "L49",
   "file": "vo/L49.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "G S T and H S T. Sales tax."
  },
  {
   "id": "L50",
   "file": "vo/L50.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "If your sales stay at or under thirty thousand dollars, in a single calendar quarter and over the last four quarters in a row, you're what the C R A calls a small supplier. You don't have to register."
  },
  {
   "id": "L51",
   "file": "vo/L51.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Go over thirty thousand, and you have to register, start charging G S T or H S T, and send it to the C R A. Once you're required to, you have twenty-nine days to register."
  },
  {
   "id": "L52",
   "file": "vo/L52.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Maya, at fourteen thousand, is a small supplier."
  },
  {
   "id": "L53",
   "file": "vo/L53.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "But if her photography grows to three thousand dollars a month, she would cross the line in less than a year. That's the moment to watch."
  },
  {
   "id": "L54",
   "file": "vo/L54.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "You can also register voluntarily. Then you charge the tax, but you may be able to claim back the G S T or H S T you paid on business expenses."
  },
  {
   "id": "L55",
   "file": "vo/L55.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Registering also means filing G S T or H S T returns. It's extra paperwork, so decide on purpose."
  },
  {
   "id": "L56",
   "file": "vo/L56.mp3",
   "gap": 1.0,
   "text": "Here's your side hustle checklist."
  },
  {
   "id": "L57",
   "file": "vo/L57.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "One. Report all of it, slip or no slip, on form T twenty-one twenty-five."
  },
  {
   "id": "L58",
   "file": "vo/L58.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Two. Keep every receipt. You're taxed on profit, not sales."
  },
  {
   "id": "L59",
   "file": "vo/L59.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Three. Set aside money every month. Nobody withholds it for you."
  },
  {
   "id": "L60",
   "file": "vo/L60.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Four. Remember April thirtieth for payment, even if you file in June."
  },
  {
   "id": "L61",
   "file": "vo/L61.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Five. Watch the thirty thousand dollar line for G S T and H S T."
  },
  {
   "id": "L62",
   "file": "vo/L62.mp3",
   "gap": 1.0,
   "text": "So, what did we learn?"
  },
  {
   "id": "L63",
   "file": "vo/L63.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "One. Side hustle profit is taxable, however you're paid."
  },
  {
   "id": "L64",
   "file": "vo/L64.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Two. It's taxed at your top rate, because it sits on top of your job."
  },
  {
   "id": "L65",
   "file": "vo/L65.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Three. Expenses reduce the bill, but only with records."
  },
  {
   "id": "L66",
   "file": "vo/L66.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Four. Nothing is withheld, so plan for the bill, and for C P P."
  },
  {
   "id": "L67",
   "file": "vo/L67.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Next on this channel: what happens when you work two jobs in Canada. Subscribe, so you don't miss it."
  }
 ],
